--!strict

-- Every monster (GDD "Monsters", "Monster Types"), M29. One entry per
-- Enums.MonsterKind: the enum key is the monster's system Name and its
-- PublicNames entry is its DisplayName, so neither is repeated here. A
-- new monster plugs in by adding its enum key and an entry; most need no
-- code at all.
-- DETECTION_RANGE_STUDS is how far it notices targets (never less than it
-- can hit from): the highest-priority one detected is walked to until it
-- is within ATTACK_RANGE_STUDS, then attacked. TARGET_PRIORITIES lists
-- what it goes for, in order; the Refinery is always first and never
-- listed. TARGET_DAMAGE_TYPES is what else its blast hurts when
-- ATTACK_RADIUS_STUDS is above 0 (its target is always hurt). A RANGED
-- monster fires PROJECTILE (a model under GameAssets/Projectiles) and its
-- radius is measured from where the projectile lands.
-- The model is the template under GameAssets/Monsters with the kind's
-- enum key as its name ("BRUTE_2"); its look and size are set on the
-- model in Studio, and its Proxy part is its hit box (decided
-- 2026-09-23). ATTACK_INTERVAL_SEC is the time between attacks (the stat
-- sheet has no rate yet; the default is GameData/Monsters/Behavior
-- DEFAULT_ATTACK_INTERVAL_SEC, and the values here are M29 placeholders).
-- Animation ids are Roblox's default R6 clips until monster art exists.
-- Every AIR monster has FLIGHT_HEIGHT_STUDS: how high above the ground its
-- feet cruise (decided 2026-09-23).
